We define the unital associative algebra $A$ generated by elements $e_1, e_2, e_3$ subject to the following relations:
\begin{align*}
& e_i^2 = e_i, \quad e_i e_j = q_{ij} e_j e_i \quad \text{for } i \neq j, \\
& \sum_{i=1}^3 e_i = 1, \quad e_i e_j e_i = e_i e_j e_j = e_j e_i e_j \quad \text{for } i \neq j.
\end{align*}
A vector $v \in A$ is designated as NIL (Nilpotent) if it satisfies the condition $(1-v)^{-1}v = (1-v)^{-1}v^2$. This paper presents an algorithm capable of determining whether a given vector $v \in A$ is NIL.
